DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These functions compute the remainder of dividing _x by _y.   The  return
       value  is _x_-_n_*_y, where _n is the value _x _/ _y, rounded to the nearest in‐
       teger.  If the absolute value of _x_-_n_*_y is 0.5, _n is chosen to be even.

       These functions are  unaffected  by  the  current  rounding  mode  (see
       ffeennvv(3)).

       The ddrreemm() function does precisely the same thing.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the floating‐point remainder, _x_-_n_*_y.
       If the return value is 0, it has the sign of _x.

       If _x or _y is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If  _x  is an infinity, and _y is not a NaN, a domain error occurs, and a
       NaN is returned.

       If _y is zero, and _x is not a NaN, a domain error occurs, and a  NaN  is
       returned.

EERRRROORRSS
       See  mmaatthh__eerrrroorr(7) for information on how to determine whether an error
       has occurred when calling these functions.

       The following errors can occur:

       Domain error: _x is an infinity and _y is not a NaN
              _e_r_r_n_o is set to EEDDOOMM (but see BUGS).  An invalid  floating‐point
              exception (FFEE__IINNVVAALLIIDD) is raised.

              These functions do not set _e_r_r_n_o for this case.

       Domain error: _y is zero
              _e_r_r_n_o  is  set  to  EEDDOOMM.   An  invalid floating‐point exception
              (FFEE__IINNVVAALLIIDD) is raised.

