BBUUGGSS
       Before glibc 2.15, the call

           remainder(nan(""), 0);

       returned  a NaN, as expected, but wrongly caused a domain error.  Since
       glibc 2.15, a silent NaN (i.e., no domain error) is returned.

       Before glibc 2.15, _e_r_r_n_o was not set to EEDDOOMM for the domain error  that
       occurs when _x is an infinity and _y is not a NaN.

